# UI usability (sort / search / navigate / icons / understand / look alike)

Apply when **adding, changing, or reviewing** any user-visible UI in `sqyre-app` or `sqyre-overlay` (desktop, wasm editor, overlays, trays, dialogs, pickers, tooltips). Prefer existing helpers over one-off widgets.

**Agent behavior:** if a change or existing panel violates these principles, **warn and suggest** a concrete fix — do not refuse the work or invent large refactors unless asked. When touching a list/panel, briefly audit neighbors in the same surface.

Audience: **casual automation beginners first**. Power-user / technical controls go behind a collapsed **Advanced** section when possible — `widgets::advanced_section` / `widgets::collapsible_section` ([`tip_advanced`](crates/sqyre-app/src/action_tooltip/sections.rs) wraps the same helper inside action tooltips).

## Principles

### Sortable
- Named lists (macros, items, programs, coords, tags, …) present a **stable, predictable order** (usually display-name, case-insensitive).
- If order matters to the user, expose an obvious control (column header, sort menu, or existing domain sort) — do not rely on insertion order alone.
- Reuse `macro_meta::cmp_display_name` (macros) / `pickers::sort_by_display_name` (name/id rows) rather than ad-hoc sorts that disagree across panels.

### Searchable
- Any list that can grow beyond ~a screenful needs a **filter field** with `hint_text` (what to type) and case-insensitive match on the labels users see.
- Filter rows are **always** `widgets::search_field` (magnifier + fill-width field + optional clear ✕, stable edit id via `SearchFieldOpts`); never hand-roll an icon+`TextEdit` row. Growing dropdowns use `widgets::searchable_combo` with `SearchableComboOpts`.
- Empty / no-match bodies: `widgets::list_vacancy` / `empty_state` — never a blank void.

### Navigable (local first)
- Prefer **in-panel** keyboard behavior over new global chords. Do not steal keys while recording macros/hotkeys/chords.
- Default local list/dialog keys (when focus is in that surface):
  - **↑ / ↓** — move selection
  - **Enter** — activate / confirm primary action
  - **Esc** — cancel / close / clear selection as appropriate
  - **type-to-filter** when a search field exists (focus it on open when that is the main job, e.g. command palette)
- Keep mouse/click paths complete; keyboard is additive accessibility, not the only way.
- Mirror proven patterns: `widgets::consume_escape` (Esc closes the topmost layer only — never raw `consume_key(Escape)`), `poll_confirm_keys`, `save_cancel_row` / `confirm_window`, command palette, `var_pills`.

### Usable
- Primary actions are visible buttons/menus — not gesture- or hotkey-only.
- Destructive actions need a clear confirm (existing pending-delete / dialog patterns).
- One obvious next step on empty states (“No macros yet — create one”).
- Avoid requiring the user to know IDs, paths, or enum variant names to complete common tasks.

### Icon-first chrome; visible field names (glyphs portray, tips enrich)
- **Chrome** (toolbar, confirm, row actions, type/status badges): prefer a recognizable glyph; the plain-language name lives in the hover tip + AccessKit name. Does **not** apply to editable form field labels — those must paint a short visible name (charter clarity / Project `ui-standards.md` §8 win over tip-only field identity).
- Use shared glyph sources, not ad-hoc characters: `egui_phosphor::regular::*` (outline) and `PHOSPHOR_FILL_FAMILY` (filled, e.g. toggled state) for icons, `widgets::VectorIcon` for action-type pictures, `warn_badge` for the ⚠ corner marker.
- Field/row labels: `widgets::pair_labeled` — glyph + **visible short name** and the control share one frame and a hairline. Shared field helpers already do this. A trailing action on that control (clear, pick, record) stays inside the frame (`pair_icon` when the leading slot is not a field label). `help::label` paints `name` (Small/weak) beside the glyph and sets the accessible name; attach help prose to the control with `help::tip(resp, help)` — never tip-only field identity. Shared help strings live in `action_tooltip/help.rs` (`h::`, action-editor fields) and `help_text.rs` (`ht::`, window/panel/picker chrome). Toolbar and confirm icons stay bare glyphs.
- Icon-only actions with no paired widget (toolbar, confirm, row chrome): `widgets::icon_button` / `cancel_icon_button` / `record_icon_button` / `icon_toggle` / `IconButton::new` — `tip` is both hover text and AccessKit name. Glyph only at rest (no fill or stroke). Hover and press draw the interactive fill, same as the brand button. Do not add a resting frame around them.
- Keep **visible text** for: editable field names, user-typed names (macros, items, tags), editable values, search/filter fields, empty-state copy, primary action verbs (Save / Cancel / Edit defaults…), and glanceable mode/status (hotkey On press/On release, non-zero delay summary). No clear glyph for chrome → short text label + tooltip beats a cryptic icon.
- Tooltip wording is plain-language enrichment — same glossary rules as labels below.

### Understandable
- Labels and hints use everyday words (macro, item, click, wait) — not crate/type jargon in the UI string.
- Every non-obvious control gets hover help or a one-line hint; for icon-only **chrome**, the tooltip carries the AccessKit name. Form field identity stays visible via `help::label`.
- Errors and status text say what happened and what to try next in plain language.
- Progressive disclosure: show the common path first (identity, targets, search area, detection Output X/Y + wait/order); tuck expert thresholds, preprocess flags, alternate match methods, Nav edge cases, mask geometry under `widgets::advanced_section` (tooltips use `tip_advanced`, which wraps it). Optional *feature* groups use `widgets::collapsible_section` with the feature name — never raw `ui.collapsing`, never an Advanced nested inside another disclosure. Required / common-path fields must not live only inside default-collapsed Advanced.
- Static explanatory **prose** does not get rendered inline — it lives in `help::tip` on the labeled control. `.weak()` text is for live values (counts, resolved positions) and short visible field names beside glyphs, not long documentation.

### Consistent rendering (look alike / refactorable)
Keep surfaces **visually interchangeable**: same control kinds should look and lay out the same so refactors stay safe and screenshots/docs stay reliable.

- **Compose shared primitives** — `theme::*` (colors, framed sections, overlays), `widgets::*` (icon/controls, fields, dialogs, headers, tags), `pickers::*`, `tip_section` / `tip_wrapped_section` / `tip_advanced`. Do not copy-paste one-off spacing, strokes, or button chrome.
- **No local palettes** — use `theme::PRIMARY`, `MACRO_START`, `MACRO_STOP`, `accent_dim`, `overlay_panel_fill`, `contrast_fg`, and egui `TextStyle` / `ui.visuals()`. Avoid hard-coded `Color32::from_rgb(…)` in panel code unless adding a token in `sqyre-ui-theme` (shared with overlay) or `sqyre-app/src/theme/tokens.rs` (app-only).
- **Stable geometry** — prefer shared widths (`W_TEXT`, `W_VAR`), `fit_dialog_window` / `fit_dialog_popup` / `fill_resize_body`, and `dialog_scroll`. Obey [egui-layout-gotchas](egui-layout-gotchas.mdc); do not invent per-panel size math that drifts.
- **Match the nearest sibling** — new rows, toolbars, lists, and confirm footers should mirror an adjacent panel of the same kind (same icon size, gap, weak-count suffix, Save/Cancel row). Visual novelty needs an explicit product ask.
- **Extract on repeat** — if the same layout appears twice, lift it into `widgets` / `theme` / `tip_*` instead of diverging copies (easier refactors, fewer look bugs).
- **Never bypass capability helpers** — `var_ref_text_edit` (autocomplete keys, `${}` pills), `parent_popup` (nested-popup survival), `visible_*` bounds (UiKind-aware), the scroll/tag/button role helpers each encode a fixed regression. Raw `egui::TextEdit`/`egui::Popup`/`ui.place` is a bug vector wherever those helpers apply — a coord-chip `ui.place(TextEdit)` once silently dropped autocomplete. If a helper can't express your case, extend it (opts struct), don't drop to raw egui. Legit raw uses: leaf suggestion popups with no children, simple name/draft fields already using `text_field`/`name_edit_width`, and multiline code/YAML editors.
- **Predictable density** — vertical gaps use only the two density tiers from `sqyre_ui_theme` / `theme`: `section_gap(ui)` between sections (framed cards, `section_separator` margins — never `add_space` around it — subsection heads) and `element_gap(ui)` between element groups inside a section (and horizontal element gaps). They scale with Settings → Appearance → Spacing; do not reintroduce `add_space(SPACE_*)` for inter-block gaps. Reuse `horizontal_wrapped`/`wrapped_row` patterns from tip sections; do not mix dense custom grids next to standard framed sections without cause.
- **Gaps flex, sizes don't** — density only changes *gaps*. Point sizes (hit areas, `icon_btn_side`, card dims, `interact_size`) stay at egui defaults — never floor `interact_size` globally (it inflates every tree/list row). Narrow viewports adapt via auto-compact gaps + narrower `text_edit_width`, not by scaling spacing to resolution.
- **Button family** — pick by role, not by convenience: `dirty_action_button` for the primary save/apply, `add_button` for create, `icon_button`/`icon_toggle` for glyph actions (tip = tooltip + AccessKit name), `cancel_icon_button` for **field/selection clears** (red ✕ — never a text "Cancel"/"Clear" button), `small_button`/`Button::small()` for inline utility and `◂`/`▸` nav rows, and raw `ui.button` only inside menus and choice rows (Delete / Overwrite / Copy). Dialog cancel is **Esc-only** — `save_row` (right-aligned Save + Esc/Enter keys) replaces the old Save/Cancel pair, and pickers float their Save via `float_bottom_right`; a painted Cancel survives only where it is a real choice (`confirm_cancel_row`/`confirm_choice_row`) or Esc is captured (`dismiss_row` record modals). Clear ✕ buttons sit adjacent to the field/picker they empty. Enabled-gated icon buttons go through `ui.add_enabled(on, IconButton::new(glyph, tip, color_when_on))`; enabled-gated text utilities use `add_enabled(on, Button::new(..).small())`. Keep the `fields.rs` helper (`text_field`, `drag_field`, `combo_*`, `searchable_combo`, `search_field`) for labeled inputs — variants go through `TextFieldOpts`/`NumFieldOpts`/`SearchFieldOpts`/`SearchableComboOpts`/`VarFieldOpts`, never a `_width`-style suffix.
- **Frames in horizontal rows** — `egui::Frame::show` children inherit the parent layout: inside `ui.horizontal`/`right_to_left` content centers in the whole *remaining* height, so labels land at the bottom of an over-tall pill. Either wrap frame content in `ui.vertical` (see `tag_pill`) or allocate manually like `tree_chrome::paint_pill`.
- **Enum pickers** — ≤3 short options: `selectable_value` toggle pills (like mask Shape); more: `combo_enum`/`searchable_combo`.
- **Tooltip sourcing** — static explanation strings live in a registry: `action_tooltip/help.rs` (`h::`) for action-editor field help, `help_text.rs` (`ht::`) for everything else (windows, panels, pickers, shared widgets). Attach via `help::tip`/`help::label` or `on_hover_text(ht::CONST)`; `on_hover_text` with an inline string is reserved for dynamic/composed values (paths, counts, live previews). Do not hand-write static hover strings — the registries keep wording consistent and auditable.
- **Wrapping rows** — multi-field rows use `widgets::wrapped_row` (or `tip_wrapped_section`); every label + control (or icon + pill, thumbnail cell, …) group inside is one `widgets::wrap_unit` so wrapping never splits it. An icon paired with its control is `widgets::pair_leading` / `pair_icon` (already a wrap unit). Shared field helpers (`text_field`, `drag_field`, `combo_*`, `search_field`) use that pair. Never nest a bare `ui.horizontal` / `ui.vertical` group in a wrapping row — it overflows instead of wrapping.

### Accessible (AccessKit is on via eframe defaults)
- Icon-only buttons use `widgets::icon_button(ui, glyph, tip)`, which sets an AccessKit label. Non-interactive icon labels/indicators get a name via `help::label` or `widget_info`. Custom-painted widgets call `response.widget_info(|| WidgetInfo::labeled(..))`; a glyph is not a label (screen readers and `egui_kittest` `get_by_label` depend on it).
- Do not signal state by color alone; pair with icon/text. Text on custom fills uses `contrast_fg(bg)`.
- Request focus once on open (track a flag), not every frame; keep Tab order = add order.

### Immediate-mode hygiene
- Stable IDs: `id_salt(..)` on ScrollArea/ComboBox/CollapsingHeader inside loops; `ui.push_id(domain_id, ..)`, never a row index (sort/filter shifts state).
- No per-frame disk I/O, image decode, or large sorts/filters — cache and invalidate on change.
- Prefer `request_repaint_after(d)`; unconditional `request_repaint()` only while animating or a run is active.

## Checklist (new or touched UI)

- [ ] List/combo: sorted predictably; filter or searchable combo if the set can grow
- [ ] Empty / no-match states have plain copy
- [ ] Local ↑↓ / Enter / Esc (or documented why not) without breaking record modes
- [ ] Form field names visible at rest (`help::label` / `pair_labeled`); icon-only chrome still has tip + AccessKit name
- [ ] Beginner / common path visible; expert options collapsed by default (not Output X/Y or wait/order)
- [ ] Primary create/edit not right-click-only
- [ ] Labels, hints, and errors readable by a non-technical user
- [ ] Reused `theme::*` tokens/visuals, `widgets::*` (incl. controls), `pickers::*`, `tip_*` / `tip_advanced` (no one-off chrome/colors)
- [ ] Layout matches a sibling of the same kind; dialogs use shared fit/scroll helpers
- [ ] Icon/custom widgets labeled; stable ids in loops; no heavy per-frame work

## Out of scope unless asked

- New **global** application hotkey schemes (local panel keys first)
- Brand / theme redesigns (changing the look system itself) — consistency with the *current* system is in scope
